# ─── Semgrep ignore patterns ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Files in this list are skipped entirely by `semgrep scan`. Use ONLY
# for paths where the matched code is legitimately not production
# (test fixtures, seed scripts, dev tooling). For inline false-
# positive suppression on a single line, prefer `// nosemgrep:
# <rule-id>` in source instead — it documents the reasoning at the
# match site.

# E2E test fixtures intentionally hard-code test-account passwords so
# Playwright can log in without a credential vault. The accounts only
# exist in the local/test database (seeded by the scripts below) and
# never appear in production.
apps/web/e2e/

# Local seed scripts — populate the dev/test database with deterministic
# test users (customer + vendor + admin). Hard-coded passwords here are
# the *fixture* values, not real credentials, and the scripts are not
# bundled into any production image (Dockerfile only copies src/, dist/).
apps/api/prisma/seed-e2e-customer.ts
apps/api/prisma/seed-e2e-vendor.ts
apps/api/prisma/seed-e2e-data.ts

# Manual one-off booking-creation script for local QA — same rationale
# as the seed scripts above.
apps/api/scripts/create-test-booking.ts

# PrismaService unit test — fixtures intentionally include reserved
# URL chars in the password to assert percent-encoding works. The test
# password is constant + obviously synthetic; never reaches a real
# system. Same rationale as the seed scripts above.
apps/api/test/unit/prisma.service.spec.ts
